X: 1
T: Jolie Blonde
O: Traditional Cajun, Louisiana
N: The "Cajun national anthem": a waltz sung to a pretty blonde who has left
N: the singer for another man. First recorded as "Ma Blonde Est Partie" by
N: Amédé, Ophy and Cleoma Breaux in 1928.
N: Melody from the Digital Tradition (abc_dtrad JOLIBLON), transposed up an
N: octave for the recorder. Chords derived from the melody.
